#. Michigan's Upper Peninsula"
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/spell_learning_items/spellbooks_hedge.json
msgid ""
"This is an anthropological collection of American folk beliefs in the Upper "
"Peninsula of Michigan, consisting of stories, legends, descriptions of "
"rituals, tall tales, and anything else the author heard during his period of"
" study.  The \"Bloodstoppers\" of the title are individuals believed to be "
"able to stop the flow of blood from a wound, with an incantation or ritual "
"or sheer force of will, and the bearwalkers were allegedly sorcerers who "
"could assume the shape of a bear and cause misfortune."
msgstr ""

