msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""
msgstr[4] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "abominable renfield"
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/monsters/bloodsuckers.json
msgid ""
"A brobdingnagian Renfield, twisted through unnatural alchemies.  Their stump"
" sized legs and feet pound the earth as they move, while their claw like "
"hands to tear you apart."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/monsters/bloodsuckers.json
msgid "vampire bat"
msgid_plural "vampire bats"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""
msgstr[4] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "vampire bat"
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/monsters/bloodsuckers.json
msgid ""
"The Northern European Vampire bat, was discovered 8 years previous to the "
"Cataclysm in Lithuania.  Within those years it had spread across the entire "
"northern hemisphere.  It is larger than a regular bat and furrier allowing "
"it to remain active in the colder winters.  They do drink human and animal "
"blood as part of their sustenance.  It roosts in caves and other hollows, "
"and uses a form of echolocation to aerially navigate through tricky terrain "
"at rapid speeds."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/monsters/bloodsuckers.json
msgid "giant vampire bat"
msgid_plural "giant vampire bats"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""
msgstr[4] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "giant vampire bat"
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/monsters/bloodsuckers.json
msgid ""
"The Mega-Chiropteran Vampire (Giant Vampire Bat), began appearing 4 years "
"ago in locations with Northern European Vampire bats.  There were videos of "
"them bringing down large animals like goats and cattle before the Cataclysm "
"as well as pervasive rumors of them coming after humans."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/monsters/changeling.json
msgid "changeling wanderer"
msgid_plural "changeling wanderers"
